1
00:00:15,073 --> 00:00:17,333
You've finally come out, Dio.

2
00:00:20,453 --> 00:00:22,913
A job well done, Polnareff.

3
00:00:23,033 --> 00:00:24,950
You managed to avenge your sister.

4
00:00:25,033 --> 00:00:29,893
But what's most impressive is that you
also found the time to track me down. Ha!

5
00:00:30,273 --> 00:00:32,473
I'll gladly kill you to celebrate.

6
00:00:32,853 --> 00:00:35,441
But I think we should
start with this first.

7
00:00:40,893 --> 00:00:42,910
I'll give you a chance to rethink.

8
00:00:42,993 --> 00:00:45,333
Descend now and not only will you live,

9
00:00:45,653 --> 00:00:48,300
you'll be given the
chance to serve me again.

10
00:00:48,433 --> 00:00:50,473
Or you could choose to rise forth.

11
00:00:50,793 --> 00:00:53,205
However, you'd be ascending to your doom.

12
00:00:54,353 --> 00:00:58,633
When the two of us first met,
fear consumed me like a curse.

13
00:00:58,833 --> 00:01:02,539
It gave your evil Card blanche
to manipulate me like a puppet.

14
00:01:02,733 --> 00:01:07,413
That fear was the beginning of a
futile existence with no end in sight.

15
00:01:07,773 --> 00:01:09,597
It was a fate worse than death.

16
00:01:09,793 --> 00:01:13,734
A wretched life devoid of any desire
other than doing your bidding.

17
00:01:15,333 --> 00:01:20,510
But that fear has been eradicated,
leaving only the burning will to fight.

18
00:01:20,593 --> 00:01:23,613
I've spent 45 days traveling with Mr.

19
00:01:23,753 --> 00:01:25,930
Joestar and the others
and in honor of those who

20
00:01:26,013 --> 00:01:28,913
died on that journey I'll
never fear you again.

21
00:01:31,193 --> 00:01:36,493
My aren't we confident climb these
stairs and put that bravado to the test?

22
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:44,473
Quite the interesting decision Polnareff.

23
00:01:45,233 --> 00:01:48,230
You've backed down after
all is that your clever

24
00:01:48,313 --> 00:01:50,901
way of telling me you
want your former life?

25
00:01:58,433 --> 00:01:59,263
back.

26
00:01:59,346 --> 00:02:00,176
What in the hell?

27
00:02:00,473 --> 00:02:04,433
But I went up the stairs. I'm
sure. What happened? Problem?

28
00:02:04,853 --> 00:02:07,053
You seem to be shaken, Polnareff.

29
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:08,693
But why is that?

30
00:02:08,893 --> 00:02:12,170
Could the winds of fear have
extinguished your burning resolve?

31
00:02:12,253 --> 00:02:15,010
Perhaps the only steps you
took were in your mind.

32
00:02:15,093 --> 00:02:18,270
And in actuality, fear overrode
your Your consciousness,

33
00:02:18,353 --> 00:02:22,370
wrestling control from your brain
causing you to descend down the stairs.

34
00:02:22,453 --> 00:02:23,283
No way!

35
00:02:23,433 --> 00:02:25,962
I'm positive I just
walked up those stairs!

36
00:02:30,353 --> 00:02:31,183
What?

37
00:02:31,266 --> 00:02:32,635
Is he doing this with his stand?

38
00:02:34,353 --> 00:02:35,183
No!

39
00:02:35,266 --> 00:02:36,096
It couldn't be!

40
00:02:39,453 --> 00:02:41,493
Dio's stand is...

41
00:02:42,793 --> 00:02:44,073
...the world?!

42
00:02:45,793 --> 00:02:47,973
What am I supposed to do now?

43
00:03:14,073 --> 00:03:15,413
He is still alive.

44
00:03:15,533 --> 00:03:19,253
The devil is not gone.

45
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:20,992
He is still alive.

46
00:03:21,813 --> 00:03:22,850
He is still alive.

47
00:03:22,933 --> 00:03:26,227
We are still looking for a
place where we are still not.

48
00:03:26,353 --> 00:03:28,870
We are still alive. We are still alive.

49
00:03:28,953 --> 00:03:34,593
When we are in the end of the battle,
we are still alive. We will stop.

50
00:03:39,073 --> 00:03:42,833
The story of the story
was that we are now.

51
00:03:53,933 --> 00:04:00,053
The end of the world!

52
00:04:20,893 --> 00:04:23,033
I'm curious, Polnareff.

53
00:04:23,273 --> 00:04:26,713
Have you ever wondered what
the human soul desires most?

54
00:04:27,013 --> 00:04:28,153
Peace of mind.

55
00:04:28,873 --> 00:04:32,167
Subconsciously, all humans
wish to overcome their fears.

56
00:04:33,033 --> 00:04:33,953
They seek fame,

57
00:04:34,373 --> 00:04:39,633
money, and dominance of others, all to
obtain a sense of everlasting security.

58
00:04:40,633 --> 00:04:41,510
What a farce.

59
00:04:41,593 --> 00:04:44,713
They create bonds as a
means of self-preservation.

60
00:04:45,093 --> 00:04:49,505
They say they wish to help others,
purely for the sake of love and justice.

61
00:04:49,733 --> 00:04:52,262
But it's only to settle
their feeble minds.

62
00:04:52,933 --> 00:04:56,109
Humanity's greatest desire
is to latch on to serenity.

63
00:04:57,053 --> 00:04:58,113
So why?

64
00:04:58,353 --> 00:04:59,953
Why refuse to serve me?

65
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:02,013
What greater serenity is there?

66
00:05:02,353 --> 00:05:05,533
Return to me and all I
speak of will be yours.

67
00:05:06,153 --> 00:05:07,977
You don't want to challenge me.

68
00:05:08,153 --> 00:05:11,510
There's just no point in running
headlong into a meaningless death.

69
00:05:11,593 --> 00:05:13,593
You deserve much more.

70
00:05:14,213 --> 00:05:15,043
No!

71
00:05:15,253 --> 00:05:17,782
Am I seriously letting
him draw me back in?

72
00:05:18,093 --> 00:05:20,353
You're a talented stand user.

73
00:05:20,713 --> 00:05:22,873
It would be a shame to kill you.

74
00:05:23,493 --> 00:05:27,493
Turn your back on Joestar
and live as my right hand.

75
00:05:27,793 --> 00:05:30,973
I promise you unending peace starting now.

76
00:05:31,353 --> 00:05:32,733
I have to resist.

77
00:05:32,953 --> 00:05:36,153
Haftal, Iggy, I need your courage.

78
00:05:37,293 --> 00:05:39,233
Cut the bullshit, Dio!

79
00:05:39,373 --> 00:05:41,549
I've already stared death in the eye!

80
00:05:42,253 --> 00:05:46,673
And I'll gladly do it again, if it
helps uncover your stand's abilities!

81
00:05:49,313 --> 00:05:50,513
How disappointing.

82
00:05:56,493 --> 00:05:59,093
Time to meet your end, Polnareff!

83
00:06:00,233 --> 00:06:02,973
So that's your stand, the world! Bring it!

84
00:06:17,453 --> 00:06:19,113
It's... Mr. Joestar!

85
00:06:19,833 --> 00:06:22,233
There's no need to worry, Paul the Rep.

86
00:06:26,233 --> 00:06:27,063
Dio!

87
00:06:27,233 --> 00:06:28,813
That was Dio!

88
00:06:29,173 --> 00:06:30,073
After him!

89
00:06:30,373 --> 00:06:32,432
I have to tell you something first!

90
00:06:32,693 --> 00:06:36,810
It was only out in the open for a moment
or two, but I saw him use his stand.

91
00:06:36,893 --> 00:06:41,573
Uh, well, I didn't actually see it, but
I did feel it in a manner of speaking.

92
00:06:42,513 --> 00:06:45,530
It's complicated, but here's
the long and short of it.

93
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:47,990
I was heading up the stairs
to beat the life out of

94
00:06:48,073 --> 00:06:51,249
that bastard when suddenly
I was back where I started.

95
00:06:51,813 --> 00:06:55,190
Believe me, I know what I'm saying
doesn't make any sense at all.

96
00:06:55,273 --> 00:06:57,690
I can't wrap my head around
what happened either.

97
00:06:57,773 --> 00:07:00,353
I feel like I'm losing my mind over here.

98
00:07:00,593 --> 00:07:03,190
I'm sure he wasn't using
any sort of hypnosis.

99
00:07:03,273 --> 00:07:06,033
I'd say super speed, but there's no way.

100
00:07:06,893 --> 00:07:10,273
All I know is that I sense
something utterly terrifying.

101
00:07:13,073 --> 00:07:15,413
Hey, where are Iggy and Abdel?

102
00:07:19,253 --> 00:07:21,813
They didn't make it. They're both dead.

103
00:07:23,293 --> 00:07:25,873
They died trying to save me.

104
00:07:32,313 --> 00:07:33,653
Is that so?

105
00:07:38,613 --> 00:07:39,533
We should go.

106
00:07:40,153 --> 00:07:40,983
Look, Mr.

107
00:07:41,066 --> 00:07:42,290
Joestar, the sun is setting.

108
00:07:42,373 --> 00:07:43,203
Let's hurry.

109
00:07:44,633 --> 00:07:45,751
Yeah, you're right.

110
00:07:46,893 --> 00:07:48,246
All right, out with it.

111
00:07:48,373 --> 00:07:50,197
What's waiting for us upstairs?

112
00:07:51,193 --> 00:07:52,153
The towers!

113
00:07:52,753 --> 00:07:54,630
There's also another room at the top!

114
00:07:54,713 --> 00:07:56,710
It's where Lord Dio dwells during the day!

115
00:07:56,793 --> 00:07:58,630
Is there another staircase to the tower?

116
00:07:58,713 --> 00:08:01,750
No, this is the only set
of stairs that leads there!

117
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:03,633
In that case, lead the way.

118
00:08:23,613 --> 00:08:25,013
So that's him.

119
00:08:25,993 --> 00:08:27,993
The two of us have never met.

120
00:08:28,273 --> 00:08:32,332
But I've known about this monster
for longer than I care to remember.

121
00:08:32,473 --> 00:08:34,653
How could I not know this fiend?

122
00:08:35,333 --> 00:08:39,921
The thought of him has been burned into
my mind ever since the day I was born.

123
00:08:40,053 --> 00:08:41,313
Same for Jotaro.

124
00:08:42,173 --> 00:08:46,433
We'd hoped this day would never come,
that we'd never have to face Dio.

125
00:08:46,713 --> 00:08:50,593
But as Joestars, we knew we'd
eventually have to destroy him.

126
00:08:51,273 --> 00:08:52,673
I have no regrets.

127
00:08:53,353 --> 00:08:55,730
I came on this journey
of my own free will,

128
00:08:55,813 --> 00:08:58,973
so I can live with whatever
happens from here on out.

129
00:08:59,953 --> 00:09:02,090
I've never seen things more clearly.

130
00:09:02,173 --> 00:09:05,470
Finally, it's like a light of
clarity has washed over me.

131
00:09:05,553 --> 00:09:08,513
My friends are that light,
while Dio is darkness.

132
00:09:09,413 --> 00:09:13,153
My body may be broken and battered,
but the fear has vanished.

133
00:09:13,873 --> 00:09:16,193
Virtue and light has purified my soul.

134
00:09:17,773 --> 00:09:20,610
We'll attack the moment Dio
steps out of the coffin.

135
00:09:20,693 --> 00:09:21,752
Stay at the ready.

136
00:09:21,993 --> 00:09:24,817
We don't know what tricks
he has up his sleeves.

137
00:09:26,333 --> 00:09:27,673
It's time, loser.

138
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:29,074
Open the coffin.

139
00:09:30,193 --> 00:09:31,023
Ugh!

140
00:09:31,106 --> 00:09:34,993
Whatever happens ordeal, you have
to know I never betrayed you!

141
00:09:35,433 --> 00:09:37,950
I only led these
degenerates here because I

142
00:09:38,033 --> 00:09:40,910
knew you had the power to
easily dispose of them!

143
00:09:40,993 --> 00:09:44,010
As certain as a man wetting
himself when pissing in the wind,

144
00:09:44,093 --> 00:09:47,073
your victory is assured
you are all-powerful!

145
00:09:47,353 --> 00:09:49,233
Please don't be angry with me!

146
00:09:49,553 --> 00:09:50,870
Enough of the groveling!

147
00:09:50,953 --> 00:09:52,373
Open the damn coffin!

148
00:09:54,013 --> 00:09:55,613
Please, I'm begging you!

149
00:09:55,713 --> 00:09:58,478
Give these bastards a
cruel and horrifying end!

150
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:00,863
Ordeal!

151
00:10:02,353 --> 00:10:03,753
Get ready, everyone.

152
00:10:11,133 --> 00:10:11,963
Why?

153
00:10:14,793 --> 00:10:16,893
I don't know what's going on.

154
00:10:17,073 --> 00:10:18,249
How'd I get in here?

155
00:10:18,393 --> 00:10:20,158
I was just opening the coffin!

156
00:10:20,473 --> 00:10:21,303
What the hell?

157
00:10:21,386 --> 00:10:22,216
How did he...

158
00:10:22,299 --> 00:10:24,795
My eyes were locked on
Loser Boy the entire time.

159
00:10:24,933 --> 00:10:26,650
Did anyone else see him get in the coffin?

160
00:10:26,733 --> 00:10:29,909
Wait, did someone put him
in there without us knowing?

161
00:10:30,113 --> 00:10:32,290
No, I was watching him just like you were.

162
00:10:32,373 --> 00:10:35,450
He's opening the coffin one second
and the next he's inside it.

163
00:10:35,533 --> 00:10:36,730
You're right, Polnareff.

164
00:10:36,813 --> 00:10:38,670
But I don't believe it's a mind trick.

165
00:10:38,753 --> 00:10:41,573
And it's not super speed
either. Good grief.

166
00:10:41,893 --> 00:10:43,540
Is he playing games with us?

167
00:10:46,613 --> 00:10:47,953
Get out of here!

168
00:10:49,753 --> 00:10:50,793
Damn you!

169
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:53,173
What are you doing? Come on!

170
00:10:57,273 --> 00:10:58,573
Let me go!

171
00:11:01,693 --> 00:11:04,213
Okay, what was that feeling back there?

172
00:11:04,413 --> 00:11:07,310
The ominous presence it was
giving off was far more powerful

173
00:11:07,393 --> 00:11:10,190
than any stand our group
has ever encountered before!

174
00:11:10,273 --> 00:11:12,710
It was like knowing a
bulldozer is coming after

175
00:11:12,793 --> 00:11:15,170
you just from the sound
of its roaring engine!

176
00:11:15,253 --> 00:11:16,693
Yeah, I sensed it too!

177
00:11:17,013 --> 00:11:18,793
An insane lust to kill us!

178
00:11:18,953 --> 00:11:21,894
It felt like somebody
shoving an icicle up my ass!

179
00:11:22,013 --> 00:11:26,837
If we hadn't escaped when we did, whatever
that was would have killed us for sure!

180
00:11:40,593 --> 00:11:41,423
Damn it.

181
00:11:41,653 --> 00:11:42,888
Just look at the sun.

182
00:11:43,173 --> 00:11:45,232
It's almost gone below the horizon.

183
00:11:45,973 --> 00:11:48,326
Dio will have the advantage in the dark.

184
00:11:50,373 --> 00:11:52,373
Hang on. Come again?

185
00:11:52,633 --> 00:11:55,590
Please don't tell me you guys are
planning to run away and hide until dawn.

186
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:57,533
Listen to me, Mr. Joestar.

187
00:11:57,913 --> 00:11:59,031
I'm finishing this.

188
00:11:59,233 --> 00:12:01,810
There's no way I'm packing
up and heading for the hills.

189
00:12:01,893 --> 00:12:02,723
You're right.

190
00:12:02,813 --> 00:12:05,107
We have to see this through to the end.

191
00:12:08,293 --> 00:12:13,117
I want to get this over with as much as
you do, but the tied up battle has turned.

192
00:12:13,373 --> 00:12:16,253
While not up close, we
face to stand the world,

193
00:12:16,453 --> 00:12:19,050
but we still have no
idea what its powers are.

194
00:12:19,133 --> 00:12:20,650
We're fighting blind here.

195
00:12:20,733 --> 00:12:21,670
Think of it this way.

196
00:12:21,753 --> 00:12:23,830
It's like mountain climbing
without knowing the route.

197
00:12:23,913 --> 00:12:26,853
If we try to fight Dio
right now, we'll all die!

198
00:12:27,333 --> 00:12:31,853
That fact is as inevitable as burping
after knocking back a couple of colas!

199
00:12:33,233 --> 00:12:36,057
Dio would be a fool not
to come racing after us,

200
00:12:36,233 --> 00:12:38,645
but he only has until sunrise to kill us!

201
00:12:38,813 --> 00:12:39,710
In the meantime,

202
00:12:39,793 --> 00:12:43,710
we need to learn the extent of his stance
power and find a way to put him down!

203
00:12:43,793 --> 00:12:46,373
If we can just hold
out until then… No way!

204
00:12:46,593 --> 00:12:48,393
I'm not going back on my word!

205
00:12:48,753 --> 00:12:51,250
Avdol and Iggy died
because of my weakness!

206
00:12:51,333 --> 00:12:53,070
I have to kill Dio.

207
00:12:53,153 --> 00:12:55,293
I'll go to hell and back to do it,

208
00:12:55,533 --> 00:12:59,353
but what I won't do is run
away from my obligation No,

209
00:12:59,593 --> 00:13:01,713
come back pull the wrap forget it.

210
00:13:01,873 --> 00:13:03,933
He's not gonna listen Jotaro.

211
00:13:04,313 --> 00:13:06,372
What do you think we should do now?

212
00:13:08,793 --> 00:13:14,530
He went down there to fight Dio as
we retreat will also be fighting him.

213
00:13:14,613 --> 00:13:18,693
Which means we'll be attacking
from both sides at once!

214
00:13:23,753 --> 00:13:25,850
Hey, buddy, let us buy this truck off you.

215
00:13:25,933 --> 00:13:26,874
What do you say?

216
00:13:27,033 --> 00:13:28,621
The hell is wrong with you?

217
00:13:28,713 --> 00:13:31,313
This baby's my bread and butter! No, wait!

218
00:13:31,473 --> 00:13:32,373
It's all yours.

219
00:13:35,193 --> 00:13:36,533
Buckle up, cock-o-een.

220
00:13:54,193 --> 00:13:55,833
There you are, Dio.

221
00:13:56,113 --> 00:13:57,810
Think I'll just run till dawn?

222
00:13:57,893 --> 00:13:59,690
You've crossed the wrong Frenchman.

223
00:13:59,773 --> 00:14:02,126
I'll settle this on my own if I have to.

224
00:14:02,313 --> 00:14:05,019
So what if I don't know
how Dio's stand works?

225
00:14:05,693 --> 00:14:07,910
I'll just find another way to defeat him.

226
00:14:07,993 --> 00:14:08,873
He's dead!

227
00:14:10,893 --> 00:14:12,070
Hold it, Polnareff.

228
00:14:12,153 --> 00:14:16,710
I had them let you go cause convincing
stubborn guys like you is a pain in the ass.

229
00:14:16,793 --> 00:14:20,790
But the old men in Kakyoin insisted
I stay close and watch your back.

230
00:14:20,873 --> 00:14:21,830
So here I am.

231
00:14:21,913 --> 00:14:23,253
Totoro!

232
00:14:24,633 --> 00:14:26,473
Oh, good grief.

233
00:14:47,433 --> 00:14:49,010
The automobile.

234
00:14:49,093 --> 00:14:51,293
Such impressive power and speed.

235
00:14:52,113 --> 00:14:55,819
When I was young, all we had were
shabby horse-drawn carriages.

236
00:14:56,233 --> 00:14:57,063
Don't move!

237
00:14:57,373 --> 00:14:58,790
What do you think you're doing?

238
00:14:58,873 --> 00:15:00,330
This car belongs to U .S.

239
00:15:00,413 --> 00:15:01,243
Senator Mr.

240
00:15:01,326 --> 00:15:04,017
Phillips, and touching
it results in a beatdown!

241
00:15:07,713 --> 00:15:09,793
What the hell is wrong with you?

242
00:15:13,613 --> 00:15:14,573
My, my.

243
00:15:14,833 --> 00:15:18,127
Young people these days are
so full of piss and vinegar.

244
00:15:18,233 --> 00:15:19,693
Times are a-changin'.

245
00:15:22,013 --> 00:15:22,843
Ah!

246
00:15:22,953 --> 00:15:23,953
Why wouldn't you?

247
00:15:24,393 --> 00:15:27,158
Stop talking now and
proceed to the front seat.

248
00:15:27,453 --> 00:15:28,571
It's time to drive.

249
00:15:28,913 --> 00:15:30,810
Just who the hell are you, Seiko?

250
00:15:30,893 --> 00:15:35,230
After I'm finished with you, you'll rue
the day you ever march into my vehicle.

251
00:15:35,313 --> 00:15:36,973
Yeah, this is unforgivable.

252
00:15:37,473 --> 00:15:40,030
No one gets away with doing
something like this to me.

253
00:15:40,113 --> 00:15:42,890
I was valedictorian in both
high school and college,

254
00:15:42,973 --> 00:15:45,230
not to mention captain of
the college wrestling team.

255
00:15:45,313 --> 00:15:47,690
Even after graduation,
people respected me.

256
00:15:47,773 --> 00:15:49,150
That's how I became a politician.

257
00:15:49,233 --> 00:15:50,063
I...

258
00:15:50,146 --> 00:15:52,490
I own a villa on a thousand-acre
plot of land in Hawaii.

259
00:15:52,573 --> 00:15:55,050
My gorgeous model of a
wife is 25 years younger,

260
00:15:55,133 --> 00:15:57,368
and I pay more taxes than anyone else!

261
00:15:57,593 --> 00:16:00,430
I've destroyed every enemy
who's ever stood in my way,

262
00:16:00,513 --> 00:16:02,250
and someday I'll become president!

263
00:16:02,333 --> 00:16:04,653
I'm THE Senator Phillips, damn it!

264
00:16:05,413 --> 00:16:07,673
Listen to me, you punk band reject!

265
00:16:07,973 --> 00:16:11,710
I'm gonna make sure you rot in prison
for the rest of your miser - Hear this,

266
00:16:11,793 --> 00:16:13,113
as I won't repeat it.

267
00:16:16,013 --> 00:16:17,353
Drive the car.

268
00:16:20,433 --> 00:16:22,315
This psychopath's gonna kill me!

269
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:24,810
I have to get the hell out of this car.

270
00:16:24,893 --> 00:16:26,433
If I don't, I'm a goner!

271
00:16:27,633 --> 00:16:28,913
Someone help me!

272
00:16:31,653 --> 00:16:33,493
What the hell?

273
00:16:38,073 --> 00:16:38,903
What's that?

274
00:16:39,133 --> 00:16:41,010
I'm positive I jumped out of the car!

275
00:16:41,093 --> 00:16:43,490
So what the hell am I
doing back in the car?

276
00:16:43,573 --> 00:16:44,913
I don't get it!

277
00:16:45,393 --> 00:16:46,653
What's going on?

278
00:16:46,793 --> 00:16:49,093
Your job is to catch up to that truck.

279
00:16:49,233 --> 00:16:51,613
Fail to do so, and you die.

280
00:16:52,313 --> 00:16:53,413
Yes, sir!

281
00:16:53,913 --> 00:16:55,873
How am I still in the car?

282
00:16:56,193 --> 00:16:57,913
Of course. That's it.

283
00:16:58,053 --> 00:16:58,913
I'm a senator.

284
00:16:59,313 --> 00:17:01,093
What can't I do? Yes!

285
00:17:01,233 --> 00:17:02,704
It makes total sense now!

286
00:17:11,553 --> 00:17:14,433
I still sense Dio's sinister bloodlust.

287
00:17:14,693 --> 00:17:16,399
Its presence is overwhelming.

288
00:17:16,833 --> 00:17:18,290
He's coming for us.

289
00:17:18,373 --> 00:17:20,667
You can bet your ass he's on our trail.

290
00:17:20,893 --> 00:17:24,364
Are you saying that Dio somehow
knows our precise location?

291
00:17:24,773 --> 00:17:25,603
Not quite.

292
00:17:25,873 --> 00:17:29,049
He stole the body of my
grandfather, Jonathan Joestar.

293
00:17:29,573 --> 00:17:33,455
I can sense his body, but I can't
tell if he's nearby or far away.

294
00:17:33,633 --> 00:17:37,339
I have a general feeling, but I
don't know exactly where he is.

295
00:17:37,533 --> 00:17:39,230
It's like when we got to Cairo,

296
00:17:39,313 --> 00:17:42,590
and while I knew he was here,
I couldn't pinpoint his lair.

297
00:17:42,673 --> 00:17:45,050
Lucky for us, the same thing goes for Dio.

298
00:17:45,133 --> 00:17:47,010
All he knows is that we're nearby,

299
00:17:47,093 --> 00:17:50,093
but he's unable to tell
the difference between us.

300
00:17:50,773 --> 00:17:54,773
And he probably doesn't know we've
separated, which is good for now.

301
00:17:56,973 --> 00:17:58,855
Why the hell isn't this working?

302
00:17:59,073 --> 00:18:02,779
Cars always start up when they
do this kind of thing in movies.

303
00:18:07,513 --> 00:18:09,454
Seems like there's a traffic jam.

304
00:18:10,053 --> 00:18:11,193
I'm sorry, sir.

305
00:18:11,373 --> 00:18:13,630
The evening commute is
always bumper to bumper.

306
00:18:13,713 --> 00:18:14,543
Move it.

307
00:18:14,626 --> 00:18:16,253
But we're stuck here.

308
00:18:16,473 --> 00:18:18,238
There's just too much traffic.

309
00:18:18,753 --> 00:18:20,710
Have you forgotten there's a sidewalk?

310
00:18:20,793 --> 00:18:22,213
Use it. The sidewalk?

311
00:18:22,493 --> 00:18:25,310
But it's covered with people
heading home from work.

312
00:18:25,393 --> 00:18:27,273
And your point? Go.

313
00:18:27,873 --> 00:18:28,813
Yes, sir.

314
00:18:31,173 --> 00:18:32,003
Faster.

315
00:18:32,113 --> 00:18:33,173
Yes, sir!

316
00:18:41,353 --> 00:18:44,570
Okay it's running hurry
up and get on Polnareff

317
00:18:44,653 --> 00:18:51,450
oh yeah oh the things i

318
00:18:51,533 --> 00:18:53,230
do for you but i've done

319
00:18:53,313 --> 00:18:55,130
everything you've asked
so you'll spare my life

320
00:18:55,213 --> 00:18:58,037
right there's no need to
kill a helpless senator

321
00:18:58,533 --> 00:18:59,363
Wrong.

322
00:19:02,333 --> 00:19:03,653
I have to be dreaming.

323
00:19:03,933 --> 00:19:05,470
What other explanation is there?

324
00:19:05,553 --> 00:19:07,906
As if a senator like me could be killed.

325
00:19:08,353 --> 00:19:09,753
It's just a dream!

326
00:19:11,213 --> 00:19:12,093
Found you.

327
00:19:12,333 --> 00:19:13,353
Now get closer.

328
00:19:13,573 --> 00:19:14,970
We need to catch up to them.

329
00:19:15,053 --> 00:19:17,833
I can't use the world
if I'm this far away.

330
00:19:18,633 --> 00:19:19,913
Look, here he comes.

331
00:19:20,213 --> 00:19:21,293
You see that car?

332
00:19:21,493 --> 00:19:22,733
That's Dio's ride.

333
00:19:25,133 --> 00:19:25,963
Hakuin!

334
00:19:29,573 --> 00:19:30,813
It's Kakyoinz.

335
00:19:30,993 --> 00:19:32,213
Take this, Dio!

336
00:19:32,513 --> 00:19:33,693
Emerald Splash!

337
00:19:51,533 --> 00:19:52,363
Unbelievable!

338
00:19:52,773 --> 00:19:55,370
He deflected my attack
with the flick of a finger!

339
00:19:55,453 --> 00:19:56,733
He barely moved!

340
00:19:57,293 --> 00:19:58,764
But how do you like this?

341
00:20:03,673 --> 00:20:07,353
He even dodged the
concentrated splash? Damn it!

342
00:20:09,593 --> 00:20:11,475
When did he bring out his stand?

343
00:20:11,633 --> 00:20:13,339
How could I have missed that?

344
00:20:17,893 --> 00:20:19,153
Well, that's a shame.

345
00:20:19,273 --> 00:20:20,567
He's too far away now.

346
00:20:21,173 --> 00:20:24,644
My punch seems to have thrown
him out of the world's range.

347
00:20:26,933 --> 00:20:27,763
Ah!

348
00:20:27,933 --> 00:20:28,933
What's happening?

349
00:20:29,533 --> 00:20:33,533
And what precisely would I gain by
explaining this situation to you?

350
00:20:33,813 --> 00:20:35,931
Pay attention to the road and drive.

351
00:20:40,533 --> 00:20:42,193
Be careful, Kakyoin.

352
00:20:42,413 --> 00:20:44,473
You were way too close to it.

353
00:20:44,713 --> 00:20:46,173
Please, forgive me.

354
00:20:46,533 --> 00:20:48,173
I didn't mean...

355
00:20:49,673 --> 00:20:52,350
It was only a few months
ago when Dio asked

356
00:20:52,433 --> 00:20:55,139
me if I was really going
to vomit out of fear.

357
00:20:55,413 --> 00:20:58,707
That monster had the audacity
to tell me I should relax.

358
00:20:59,913 --> 00:21:00,743
Bastard!

359
00:21:00,826 --> 00:21:01,656
Never again!

360
00:21:01,739 --> 00:21:03,219
I'll never lose to you again!

361
00:21:03,573 --> 00:21:05,213
Are you alright, Kakyoin?

362
00:21:05,393 --> 00:21:07,569
Did you catch a glimpse of the world?

363
00:21:07,733 --> 00:21:11,573
Yes, I saw it when I attacked
Dio from ten meters away.

364
00:21:11,833 --> 00:21:14,550
If I had gotten any closer,
I would have been done for.

365
00:21:14,633 --> 00:21:16,630
But we know one thing for certain.

366
00:21:16,713 --> 00:21:20,850
His stand holds a power more horrific
than we could have ever imagined.

367
00:21:20,933 --> 00:21:23,109
However, we know two things about it.

368
00:21:23,733 --> 00:21:24,563
First,

369
00:21:24,646 --> 00:21:27,950
his stand doesn't have the reach of my
Hierophant Green or your Hermit Purple.

370
00:21:28,033 --> 00:21:29,857
It's a close-range power stand,

371
00:21:30,053 --> 00:21:33,288
like Star Platinum, and has
a range of about 10 meters.

372
00:21:33,533 --> 00:21:34,363
Second,

373
00:21:34,446 --> 00:21:38,742
it attacked with its fist, so it doesn't
use projectile weapons like bullets.

374
00:21:38,913 --> 00:21:39,993
That being said,

375
00:21:40,233 --> 00:21:42,670
if we can sneak up on
him and get within range,

376
00:21:42,753 --> 00:21:45,250
we just might have a chance
of finishing him off.

377
00:21:45,333 --> 00:21:47,393
We have to figure out his secret.

378
00:21:47,513 --> 00:21:51,993
Even so, we have to exercise extreme
caution when approaching this bastard.

379
00:21:53,393 --> 00:21:54,473
Hold on.

380
00:21:54,753 --> 00:21:56,393
Why does car suddenly stop?

381
00:22:00,813 --> 00:22:01,643
Incoming!

382
00:22:01,853 --> 00:22:03,147
We're about to be hit!

383
00:22:08,273 --> 00:22:09,613
Mr. Joestar!

384
00:22:37,133 --> 00:22:39,113
What are you doing, Kakyoin?

385
00:22:39,353 --> 00:22:40,773
I understand now.

386
00:22:42,673 --> 00:22:46,053
I know now how to uncover
the secret of Dio's stand.

387
00:23:02,793 --> 00:23:04,533
Thank you.

388
00:23:27,793 --> 00:23:30,028
Whenever I think about Avdol and Iggy,

389
00:23:30,113 --> 00:23:33,330
it makes the hairs on the
back of my neck stand on end.

390
00:23:33,413 --> 00:23:36,990
I'm sure it's because they were the
first to treat me like a friend.

391
00:23:37,073 --> 00:23:39,955
My friends and I were on
a journey to defeat Dio.

392
00:23:40,313 --> 00:23:42,153
All right, here it comes!
